WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:02.389
Napoleon Dynamite took the world by storm.

00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:07.140
For what seemed like years, an entire generation
couldn't stop making jokes about ligers, llamas,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.500
and sweet skills.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.020
But what's become of Jon Heder, the man who
wore the iconic "Vote for Pedro" t-shirt?

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.440
A lot, as it turns out.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.300
Throughout much of his career, Heder has been
been known to get positively weird.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.140
He's appeared in all manner of bizarre web
productions, side projects, and short films.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.520
From Robot Chicken to Buddy Holly is Alive
and Well on Ganymede, his range of expression

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.400
and delivery has added the perfect touch of
surrealism to many productions.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.840
But there is no work that more encapsulates
this facet of his filmography than Sockbaby.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.720
A four-part action comedy series, Sockbaby
is a hallucinatory spoof of everything from

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.040
Blaxploitation to classic sci-fi.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.740
It's the kind of thing you get introduced
to in college and then quote obsessively for

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.580
years afterward.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.620
Heder plays the leader of the dastardly Frogmen,
who promptly gives birth to his own doppelganger.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.280
In real life, Heder is a kind-hearted family
man, but on screen, he's far from afraid of

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.280
the truly bizarre.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.960
It's not all glitz, glamour, and weird online
comedy for Heder.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.820
He seems to mostly love his life as a typical
family man more than anything else.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.780
He married fellow Brigham Young University
alumnus Kirsten Bales in 2002, and they're

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.640
raising four children together in their California
home.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.520
Heder's Instagram features plenty of highlights
of fatherly joy: from helping out with Halloween

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.180
costumes, to petting llamas, to the Heder
family getting their Nintendo on.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.720
Though Heder has worked steadily for years
now and shows no signs of stopping, it's clear

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.760
that his home life is very much the sun around
which he orbits.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.540
He lives a quiet life by Hollywood standards,
and it seems to suit him just fine.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.820
Though his career has extended far beyond
Vote for Pedro t-shirts and jokes about "skills,"

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.900
Heder isn't averse to revisiting his signature
performance.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.360
On screen, he reprised the role of Napoleon
in a Robot Chicken sketch and recorded a number

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:51.960
of commercials with Pedro himself, Efren Ramirez,
to promote the 2005 Utah State Fair.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:52.620
"Who won?"

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:53.560
"What?"

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:54.960
"Who won the battle?"

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.700
"Do you see any flippin' Sasquatches around
here?"

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:03.500
Plus, in 2014, Heder played the part of "Napoleon
Bonafrog" on Nickelodeon's Teenage Mutant

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.440
Ninja Turtles.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.360
This is to say nothing of the many interviews
in which, in the middle of promoting something

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.200
entirely different, he's asked to perform
a famous line.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.100
"Hey Napoleon, did you wet the bed last night?"

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.340
"Hey Dawn, did you take a dump in your bed
last night?"

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.500
"Dead on.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.400
That was perfect."

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.760
Happily, Heder takes it all in stride, and
he's never lost any gratitude for his iconic

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.260
role.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.680
In 2018, he told the Herald-Tribune,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.620
"Parents are introducing it to their kids,
friends are introducing it to their younger

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.920
friends, 14 years since it came out.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.690
I think it will always relate to youth culture
and the awkwardness of being young and being

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.000
on your own without any responsibility."

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.180
In the years since Napoleon Dynamite, Heder
has been presented with plenty of opportunities.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:48.099
He keeps the details to himself for the most
part, but it's clear that he's turned down

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:52.050
more than a few chances to be part of some
projects that ended up going the distance.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:56.700
While some might see this as foolish, Heder
considers it an asset: because of his early

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.879
work, he can pick and choose exactly what
kind of work he wants to do and figure out

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.480
a work-life balance few actors get to have.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.140
In 2012, he told Vulture,

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.640
"I realized how happy I am trying to be somewhat
normal without becoming huge.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.010
And not so much normal, but grounded, down-to-earth."

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.239
He also compared his work to that of his father,
a family doctor.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:19.180
The two professions may appear quite different,
but Heder's always wanted the same level of

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.820
community and quiet in his life.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.200
This affords him the option of saying no to
projects he finds distasteful, like raunchy

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:25.720
comedies.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:30.019
Though he's not strayed too far from his comedy
roots, Heder does dip a toe into the world

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:33.459
of dramatic film now and then, especially
the independent ones.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:37.810
In recent years he's appeared in the relationship
drama Weepah Way for Now, the Walt Disney

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:43.130
biopic Walt Before Mickey, and For Ellen,
a downbeat story of divorce and creative failure.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.790
Heder's been fairly tight-lipped about this
stage of his career.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.900
Perhaps it's an experiment he's still waiting
to see the results of, or a new direction

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:50.400
entirely.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.560
Regardless, it's a pleasure to see him do
his thing as an actor, especially when he's

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.320
pushed to take his skills to new emotional
places.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:02.360
Beyond Heder's role in one of the biggest
sleeper hits of the 21st century and his continued

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.659
passion for the performing arts, one of the
most important parts of his life is his foundation

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.660
in the Mormon church.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:12.220
His entire life has been shaped by his faith,
from his time at Brigham Young University

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.069
to his choosiness when it comes to what projects
he's part of.

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:18.099
When asked of the effects of his upbringing
on his career, he told Vulture,

00:04:18.099 --> 00:04:22.759
"These are the standards I live by and whatever
comes my way in the future, whether filmmaking

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.560
or animation or whatever, I'm going to do
my best to live by those standards."

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.289
Regardless of fame, fortune, or fairweather
friends, Heder will always have those grounding

00:04:31.289 --> 00:04:32.580
principles to guide him.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.380
If the future is like the past, they should
take him far.

